From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: trigger L1 SER on stuck TX tokens

A TX token that firmware never returns stays in the host token table
until a reset. Enough of them block transmission for every station on
a band. Age alone does not mark such a token, because firmware holds
the frames of a sleeping station until it wakes or leaves. A client
that roams away without a deauth postpones its removal past the
normal age. On MT7986, the host flag of a station does not show power
save, because firmware reports only a wake.

The driver checks its token table every 10 s and requests an L1 SER
for the band of its oldest token older than 420 s. A token of a
station whose hardware table entry shows power save counts only after
twice that age. The check runs under RCU without a lock, so it never
stalls TX, and its deadlines assume 64-bit jiffies. Two debugfs files
set the normal age, which scales the other, and turn SER off for a
log-only run. A PLE hang SER arms the check hold-off, and a request
sends only the trigger, because a SER mask command replaces the
firmware recovery mask. Each stale token line names queue and frame
control from the token record, because the scan must not read a frame
without the token lock.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
